  "final_text": "I finished all four steps and read the results back from Kibana to confirm them.\n\n1. **Data view 'Kibana Sample Data Logs'** (id `90943e30-\u2026`, index `kibana_sample_data_logs`): its time field is `timestamp`. It also has `@timestamp` and `utc_time` date fields. The main fields are:\n   - **Request details:** `request`, `url`, `extension`, `referer`\n   - **HTTP response code:** `response`, a text field with a `response.keyword` version used for grouping and filtering\n   - **Size:** `bytes`\n   - **Client and location:** `clientip`, `ip`, `geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`\n   - **Machine and host:** `machine.os`, `machine.ram`, `host`, `agent`\n   - **Other:** `memory`, `phpmemory`, `tags`, `message`, `hour_of_day`\n\n2. **Dashboard 'S4-c771f640 Web logs'** (id `af0ea3aa-c287-44a7-b634-372f294fb372`) has exactly two panels, both on that data view:\n   - \"Requests over time\": a line chart counting requests per time interval on `timestamp`.\n   - A pie chart counting requests by `response.keyword`, showing up to 10 codes.\n\n3. **Rule 'S4-c771f640 5xx errors'** (id `c2c7fffe-74a2-45ef-bdcf-8a037f86fd62`) is an Elasticsearch query rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`. It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 requests with a response code from 500 to 599 arrive within 5 minutes. It was created enabled.\n   - I changed one default setting. Kibana had saved the rule with `excludeHitsFromPreviousRun` on, which makes each check skip errors an earlier check already counted. With it on, the rule would miss some errors in the 5-minute window, so I turned it off.\n   - The codes are stored as text, so the rule matches values from \"500\" up to but not including \"600\". That covers every 3-digit 5xx code. I couldn't look at the actual codes in the data because Kibana's console proxy is turned off on this instance.\n\n4. **Panel edit and rule check:** The pie panel's title is now \"Responses by code\", and the other panel is unchanged. Reading the rule back shows `enabled: true`, and its last run status is `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
